## Documentation vault (`docs/`)

If `docs/` is a symlink to an external vault, say so and note that the target is
machine-specific. General frontmatter and folder rules are in the parent file.

### Area values

`area`: `architecture` | `integrations` | `testing` | `infrastructure` | `analysis` | `general`

### Vault structure

```
docs/
├── architecture/
│   └── diagrams/
├── integrations/
├── testing/
├── analysis/
├── plans/
└── infrastructure/
```

### Where to put new files

| Content | Location | Type |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture overview | `docs/architecture/{name}.md` | reference |
| Architecture diagram | `docs/architecture/diagrams/{name}` + `.md` | reference |
| External integration | `docs/integrations/{name}.md` | reference |
| Test patterns | `docs/testing/{name}.md` | reference |
| Code analysis / audit | `docs/analysis/{name}.md` | analysis |
| Implementation plan | `docs/plans/{feature}/be-plan.md` + `fe-plan.md` | plan |
| Infra / deployment | `docs/infrastructure/{name}.md` | reference |

