## Knowledge store — project config

> The general protocol is in the parent file. Project-specific config only below.
> Fill this in for the store you actually run — `wippy-kb`, `mempalace`, `iknow`.

- **Store and version:** `<tool>`
- **This project's partition:** `<project>`
- If a code index is generated, name the command that owns it. The agent writes
  findings only and never touches the index.
- **Partitions:**
  - `<repo_1>` — code index from `<repo-1>/`
  - `<repo_n>` — code index from `<repo-n>/`
  - `documentation` — files from `docs/`
  - `decisions` — architecture and design decisions
  - `bugs` — root cause + fix + prevention
  - `general` — catch-all
- Where the partition mapping lives, and whether a subproject needs its own.
- **Re-index after large code changes** — the exact command, plus how to force-include
  a language the indexer skips by default. Both belong here verbatim: an agent will not
  reconstruct them.

<details><summary>Example, mempalace</summary>

```bash
mempalace mine <repo-1>/ --agent claude
```

Force-include an extension outside the defaults:

```bash
FILES=$(find <repo>/src -name "*.<ext>" -type f \
  | sed 's|<repo>/||' | tr '\n' ',' | sed 's/,$//') && \
  mempalace mine <repo>/ --agent claude --include-ignored "$FILES"
```

</details>

