## graphify

One graph per subproject:

| Path | Covers | Stack |
|---|---|---|
| `<repo-1>/graphify-out/` | <what> | <languages> |
| `<repo-n>/graphify-out/` | <what> | <languages> |

Rules:

- Before answering an architecture or codebase question, read the relevant
  `GRAPH_REPORT.md` for god nodes and community structure.
- If `wiki/index.md` exists in a `graphify-out/`, navigate that instead of raw files.
- After modifying code in a subproject, run the cheap AST-only rebuild there:
  ```bash
  cd <repo> && python3 -c "from graphify.watch import _rebuild_code; from pathlib import Path; _rebuild_code(Path('.'))"
  ```
  Use the interpreter recorded in `graphify-out/.graphify_python` if graphify was
  installed as a uv tool rather than into the system python.
- For larger changes (new modules, architecture shifts) prefer `/graphify-update`.
- Keep `.graphifyignore` current when adding generated or vendored directories.
- Run the first graphify once a skeleton exists, not on an empty repo.
